# UK Road Safety Analytics

## Project Overview

This project investigates road collision severity across Great Britain using official 2025 Department for Transport data.

The objective is to identify road and environmental conditions associated with serious or fatal injury collisions, explore potential safety concerns, and eventually develop a machine-learning model for collision severity classification.

## Business Problem

Transport authorities and road safety organisations need evidence to prioritise safety investigations and interventions.

This project explores how collision severity varies by lighting, weather, road surface and road characteristics.

## Data Source

Department for Transport — Road Safety Open Data (2025).

[https://www.gov.uk/government/statistical-data-sets/road-safety-open-data](https://www.gov.uk/government/statistical-data-sets/road-safety-open-data)

The dataset covers police-reported personal injury collisions on public roads in Great Britain.

